WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.250
With Jupiter Ascending out now, let’s take
a look at 11 / 12 things you probably didn’t

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.420
know about the Wachowskis’ sci-fi adventure!

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:13.400
Caine Wise may zip and zoom about on a pair
of air-surfing boots, but in reality, actor

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.610
Channing Tatum used a pair of skates on a
system of ramps, platforms and cables to give

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:23.140
the feeling of airborne movement.
With the help of 6 men pulling wires behind

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:29.180
a green screen, Tatum rollerbladed at 4 and
a half miles per hour on a giant three-sided

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.950
treadmill four metres long and two metres
wide.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.700
The wheels of the skates, of course, were
erased during post-production!

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:42.700
Pro inline skater Cory Miller from California,
and vert skater Taïg Khris from France helped

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:47.360
train Channing Tatum and the Jupiter Ascending
stunt team.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.469
Tatum had no previous rollerblading experience,
and in the beginning found it tough to skate

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:55.980
fast and still stop in time to throw or block
a punch.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.140
But according to the actor, he started to
get the hang of it when he just kept his skates

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.930
on all day!

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:08.590
Taïg Khris is best known for his 2010 drop
from the Eiffel Tower onto a vert ramp which

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.630
broke the world record for the highest inline
skate jump.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:16.340
But he also performed Caine Wise’s leap
from the second floor balcony of the Great

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:20.619
Hall in the Natural History Museum, which
doubled for Kalique’s palace.

00:01:20.619 --> 00:01:26.209
And he “flew” through Ely Cathedral, which
doubled as the chapel on Titus’ ship.

00:01:26.209 --> 00:01:32.109
Caine Wise is a genetically-engineered human
whose DNA was spliced with that of a wolf.

00:01:32.109 --> 00:01:37.289
Director Lana Wachowski discovered that real
wolves hunt in packs and that wolves exiled

00:01:37.289 --> 00:01:42.959
from the pack, as Caine was in Jupiter Ascending,
almost always die unless they become a super-hunter.

00:01:42.959 --> 00:01:48.709
Caine’s splice of wolf DNA enhances his
skills and heightens his senses.

00:01:48.709 --> 00:01:54.939
Over 1.3 million Swarovski crystals were used
on the film’s costumes.

00:01:54.939 --> 00:02:00.139
Jupiter’s white and ruby gown, for example,
features hundreds of crystals as well as hand-made

00:02:00.139 --> 00:02:03.969
flowers, and a headdress of ruby flowers and
more crystals.

00:02:03.969 --> 00:02:08.679
Also, 3D printing was used to create both
Jupiter’s headdress and some of the jewellery

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:11.299
seen in the movie.

00:02:11.299 --> 00:02:16.610
The movie’s first big action sequence, which
begins at Chicago’s Willis Tower and darts

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:21.250
under bridges and above the city’s skyline,
is a blend of physical stunts by the actors

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:27.049
and stunt doubles, practical location shots,
visual effects, and green-screen stage work.

00:02:27.049 --> 00:02:32.159
It took an amazing 8 months of planning to
carry out the aerial work in that scene.

00:02:32.159 --> 00:02:36.939
First, the Jupiter Ascending crew perfected
the stunt choreography in the safe environment

00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:39.670
of Warner Bros. Studios in Leavesden in the
UK.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:45.530
After that, they did test runs in Long Beach,
California, to confirm that performers suspended

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:51.269
from helicopters could carry out a series
of flying poses, while being filmed by cameras

00:02:51.269 --> 00:02:55.920
positioned on other helicopters.
Once filming proper began, parts of downtown

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.560
Chicago were closed and completely evacuated
in the early morning and nightfall for two

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.370
weeks.
This was so that low-level helicopters with

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:07.680
Channing Tatum and Mila Kunis’s stunt doubles
suspended from them could fly around buildings,

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:13.409
while a second helicopter filmed the action.
At the same time, a third helicopter filmed

00:03:13.409 --> 00:03:19.290
background plates for the hundreds of visual
effects shots of downtown Chicago’s destruction.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:24.840
On top of this, there were 4 camera crews
on rooftops along the route to capture additional

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.560
footage.
Because big-action chase scenes are so complicated,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.639
they’re typically shot in daylight or at
night to give filmmakers as much time as possible

00:03:33.639 --> 00:03:37.659
to get all the shots they need.
However, the Wachowskis wanted to film just

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:42.519
before sunrise to capture the unique look
and feel of that time of day.

00:03:42.519 --> 00:03:49.519
That meant their shoot had a very tight schedule;
just 30 minutes from 5.15am to 5.45am, to

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.030
be precise!

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:57.480
To capture the best action shots on location,
the movie’s visual effects supervisor Dan

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:03.819
Glass and cinematographer John Toll created
a new 6-camera rig named the Panocam, which

00:04:03.819 --> 00:04:08.099
was fixed to a helicopter.
This new rig captured super-wide angle views

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:13.249
at very high resolutions for many shots, which
they later painted their computer-generated

00:04:13.249 --> 00:04:14.569
images on to.

00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:21.569
CG creature Greeghan, who’s one of Balem’s
deadly royal guards, is a sort of 7-foot tall

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.180
lizard with a 20-foot wingspan and a whip-like
tail.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:30.490
To prepare for his motion-capture performance,
actor Ariyon Bakare, who portrays Greeghan,

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:35.630
studied the movements of lizards such as Komodo
dragons, and aimed to combine human intelligence

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:39.990
with a reptile’s agility and unpredictability.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:45.479
The design of the spaceships in Jupiter Ascending
was influenced by the history of transportation

00:04:45.479 --> 00:04:48.580
and the fact that rich people have always
travelled in style.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:53.220
The Wachowskis wanted to reflect this by giving
their spaceships a sense of opulence they

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:58.169
thought was generally missing in sci-fi movies.
The film’s various spacecraft are sleek

00:04:58.169 --> 00:05:03.710
and agile, with designs inspired by nature,
for example, insects or birds of prey.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:09.690
Production Designer Hugh Bateup adapted the
hallways and display areas at London’s Natural

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:13.340
History Museum to create the set of Kalique’s
palace.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:17.979
Later, gilded domes and spires were added
digitally.

00:05:17.979 --> 00:05:23.430
The chapel scene on Titus’s ship was filmed
at Ely Cathedral in Cambridgeshire, England.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:28.449
Production designer Hugh Bateup combined the
Cathedral’s sandstone gothic features with

00:05:28.449 --> 00:05:33.479
modern steel-framed window structures and
light fixtures created by set decorator Peter

00:05:33.479 --> 00:05:38.430
Walpole and the prop department.
As for the overall look of Titus’s home,

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:43.180
that was influenced by a variety of styles
including Gothic and Art Deco architecture,

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:47.360
as well as the huge pillars of old English
churches, and the wood finishes and brass

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.419
or gold trim of mid-19th-century luxury yachts.

00:05:51.419 --> 00:05:57.550
Balem’s home is a vast space which includes
a lab and refinery, and brings to mind both

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:01.740
a steel mill and a supercollider.
To create that world, the crew constructed

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:06.639
enormous sets at Leavesden Studios and the
visual effects team surrounded those sets

00:06:06.639 --> 00:06:12.039
with floor-to-ceiling green screens.
Balem’s world is a spin on gothic and industrial

00:06:12.039 --> 00:06:13.440
styles, with added opulence.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:18.330
Well there you have it, 12 things you probably
didn't know about Jupiter Ascending!

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:21.699
Now, tell me, what’s your favourite sci-fi
movie?

